  "questions": [
    {
      "question": "How much is it going to cost?",
      "answer": [
        "Each Cultural Graduation Celebration will cost $25 per graduate. This fee is non-refundable and will be used to cover the cost of the event, including but not limited to venue rental, decorations, and other event-related expenses."
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What do I need to submit in order to participate?",
      "answer": [
        "Submit the Cultural Graduation Application.",
        "Submit your 75-word personal narrative and picture in the application."
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is required for my application?",
      "answer": [
        "CIN",
        "Major(s)",
        "Minor(s)",
        "Certificate(s)",
        "Headshot picture (optional)",
        "75-word acknowledgment (optional)",
        "Example: I would like to thank my family and friends for their continuous support throughout my academic journey. Their encouragement and belief in me have been instrumental in helping me achieve this milestone. I am also grateful to my professors and mentors for their guidance and inspiration. This achievement is not just mine but a reflection of the collective effort and love from those around me."
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What should I wear?",
      "answer": [
        "We encourage you to wear business casual, graduation regalia, or cultural regalia."
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How many guest tickets do I get?",
      "answer": [
        "ALL Graduations are open seating (not reserved). First come, first served. Number of guest tickets may be subject to change.",
        "APIDA Grad # of Guest Tickets: TBA",
        "Black Grad # of Guest Tickets: TBA",
        "IndigiGrad # of Guest Tickets: TBA",
        "Nuestra Grad # of Guest Tickets: TBA",
        "Pride Grad # of Guest Tickets: TBA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "I have more questions. Who do I contact?",
      "answer": [
        "Please email the Cross Cultural Centers (CCC) directly at crossculturalcenters@calstatela.edu or visit the Cross Cultural Centers (CCC) located on the 2nd floor of the University-Student Union."
      ]
    }
  ],
